From 51b67a556ea8dac5365e9379bd9f77cbc7514efa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:44:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] libos/linux: Measure clock() with the process CPU-time
 clock

The generic clock() returns the sum of the times() fields, which Linux
counts in 100 Hz ticks, so dividing by CLOCKS_PER_SEC gave a value
10000 times too small. It also counted the CPU time of waited-for
children, which isn't the processor time of this process.
---
 libos/linux/clock.c     | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libos/linux/meson.build |  1 +
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libos/linux/clock.c

diff --git a/libos/linux/clock.c b/libos/linux/clock.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..313c6f40d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libos/linux/clock.c
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+/*
